<title>USA: Sara Lee raises payout, to buy back stock.</title>
<headline>Sara Lee raises payout, to buy back stock.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sara Lee Corp Chairman John Bryan said Thursday the company's board had voted to raise the quarterly dividend to $0.21 a share from $0.19.</p>
<p>The food company's board also approved the repurchase of 20 million shares, Bryan said during the annual meeting here. The repurchase is in addition to previous share buyback plans.</p>
<p>The company has about 485 million shares outstanding.</p>
<p>Record and pay dates for the higher dividend were not available.</p>
<p>-- Chicago Newsdesk 312-408-8787</p>
</text>
